\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {III}The moments needed for the target response}{2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Common-input synthetic comparison of exact and linear temperature adapters. Upper panels show physical-target coverage and finite-test Clopper--Pearson intervals; the dashed line is the nominal calibration level. Lower panels show the five-dimensional residual-ball diameter and the mean width of nonempty rest-anisotropy intervals. Empty intervals count as noncoverage and are excluded only from the explicitly labeled nonempty width means. Both methods use the same correlated temperature errors, with noiseless known monopole and higher modes. These are pointwise oracle benchmarks, not calibrated intervals for an unknown observed CMB sky.}}{3}{}}
